# Written at work item 8, run for the first time at work item 9 (D31).
#
# LLVM 23.1.0 finds 170 things to say about this core. Sixteen were real and are
# fixed in the code; the rest are excluded below and every exclusion carries a
# reason rather than a preference, because a check switched off to make a build
# quiet is a check that was never doing anything.
#
# THE FOUR ORIGINAL EXCLUSIONS, from work item 8:
#   *-magic-numbers            F' CPP-8 and CPP-30 govern constants here, and
#                              Config.hpp already names every bound with its
#                              derivation. The generic check would flag the byte
#                              offsets in ModelFile.cpp, which are the format.
#   *-avoid-c-arrays           F' forbids the STL alternatives outright (CPP-25);
#                              fixed C arrays are the required shape, not a lapse.
#   readability-identifier-length
#                              short loop indices are idiomatic in the reference
#                              this file transcribes.
#
# ADDED AT WORK ITEM 9, after seeing what the checks actually say:
#
#   misc-include-cleaner (87 findings)
#       Wants every file to include <cstdint> directly for U8, U32 and the rest.
#       That is precisely the design this core does not have: Types.hpp is the
#       single place those names come from, so that work item 9 can swap it for
#       F's own types and no other file changes (D31 consequence 2, D35). Doing
#       what this check asks would break the two-worlds build it exists to
#       protect. The check is right about C++ in general and wrong about this.
#
#   misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes (28)
#       All 28 are `struct Model`, which is a plain aggregate by design and
#       documented as one: the loader fills it and the detector reads it. Making
#       its fields private would add 30 accessors and no safety.
#
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result (28)
#       Byte offsets of the form `data + (4U * index)`, computed in U32 and
#       widened to size_t. Overflow is impossible here and the bound is not a
#       hope: every count is checked against the Config maxima before use and a
#       larger file is refused with TOO_LARGE, so the widest product this core
#       can form is 4 * MAX_PARAMETERS = 301,440, twelve bits short of U32.
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters (7)
#       Adjacent same-typed parameters -- (rows, columns), (input, output)
#       scratch pointers. The check cannot see that the golden vectors would
#       fail instantly if any pair were swapped, which is a stronger guarantee
#       than a naming convention.
#
#   readability-redundant-member-init (2)
#       Wants `m_model()` and `m_ewma()` dropped from Detector's initialiser
#       list because their default constructors run anyway. F' CPP-19 requires
#       every variable to be explicitly initialised. F' wins; the redundancy is
#       the point.
#
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity (2)
#       `ModelFile::load` scores 44 and `Baseline::step` 28 against a threshold
#       of 25. `load`'s structure IS the specification: docs/MODEL_FILE.md 8
#       fixes the order of its checks and says the order matters, so splitting
#       it would scatter a normative sequence across functions and make the one
#       property a reviewer must verify harder to verify.
#
#   misc-const-correctness (1)
#       `char** argv` in `main`. That is main's signature.
#
#   bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion / cert-err34-c (1)
#       Flags `fscanf` in DeterminismTest regardless of what follows. Its return
#       value is checked on the next line, which is what the check is asking for.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -misc-const-correctness,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion,
  -cert-err34-c,
  -readability-redundant-member-init,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: 'include/sentinel/.*'
FormatStyle: none
